{"id":"f753356251a9-0113","source":"references/pptset/【加赠】700页逻辑图形 (1).pptx","sourcePage":113,"slideXmlSha256":"653ccab46339b3406e8fb730a69cbd172f7a30f09c94abef4b1ba4d333873041","slots":[{"anchor":"s401-s393","text":"KPI\nUses","box":[0.6824,0.4956,0.0693,0.0479]},{"anchor":"s401-s394","text":"Current\nState","box":[0.6764,0.1995,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s401-s396","text":"Implemented\nSolutions","box":[0.5246,0.3541,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s401-s397","text":"Future\nState","box":[0.8278,0.3555,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s401-s398","text":"Business Objectives","box":[0.8283,0.6629,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s401-s399","text":"Quality of Requirements","box":[0.6765,0.8218,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s401-s400","text":"Proposed Solutions","box":[0.5258,0.6629,0.0811,0.0524]},{"anchor":"s404-s402","text":"A performance indicator or key performance indicator (KPI) is a type of performance measurement. KPIs evaluate the success of an organization or of a particular activity (such as projects, programs, products and other initiatives) in which it engages.\n\nOften success is simply the repeated, periodic achievement of some levels of operational goal (e.g. zero defects, 10/10 customer satisfaction), and sometimes success is defined in terms of making progress toward strategic goals. Accordingly, choosing the right KPIs relies upon a good understanding of what is important to the organization. What is deemed important often depends on the department measuring the performance – e.g. the KPIs useful to finance will differ from the KPIs assigned to sales.","box":[0.0966,0.4071,0.3457,0.4282]},{"anchor":"s404-s403","text":"Key Performance Indicators KPI Uses Structure","box":[0.0951,0.2694,0.3158,0.1107]},{"anchor":"s2","text":"Key Performance Indicators KPI Uses Structure","box":[0.0283,0.0378,0.9417,0.0673]}],"warnings":[],"stats":{"objects":35,"textBlocks":10},"reconstructedSlots":[{"anchor":"text-0","text":"KPI","box":[0.7097763687555213,0.5025514390733506,0.0145443436